,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1183.452975083,"data":"Problem: Let $n \\geq 6$ be a positive integer. We call a positive integer $n$-Norwegian if it has three distinct positive divisors whose sum is equal to $n$. Let $f(n)$ denote the smallest $n$-Norwegian positive integer. Let $M=3^{2025!}$ and for a non-negative integer $c$ define $g(c)=\\frac{1}{2025!}\\left\\lfloor \\frac{2025! f(M+c)}{M}\\right\\rfloor.$ We can write $g(0)+g(4M)+g(1848374)+g(10162574)+g(265710644)+g(44636594)=\\frac{p}{q}$ where $p$ and $q$ are coprime positive integers. What is the remainder when $p+q$ is divided by $99991$?\n"}
