,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2429.17296633,"data":"Problem: Let $ABC$ be a triangle with $AB \\neq AC$, circumcircle $\\Omega$, and incircle $\\omega$. Let the contact points of $\\omega$ with $BC$, $CA$, and $AB$ be $D$, $E$, and $F$, respectively. Let the circumcircle of $AFE$ meet $\\Omega$ at $K$ and let the reflection of $K$ in $EF$ be $K'$. Let $N$ denote the foot of the perpendicular from $D$ to $EF$. The circle tangent to line $BN$ and passing through $B$ and $K$ intersects $BC$ again at $T \\neq B$. Let sequence $(F_n)_{n \\geq 0}$ be defined by $F_0 = 0$, $F_1 = 1$ and for $n \\geq 2$, $F_n = F_{n-1} + F_{n-2}$. Call $ABC$ $n$-tastic if $BD = F_n$, $CD = F_{n+1}$, and $KNK'B$ is cyclic. Across all $n$-tastic triangles, let $a_n$ denote the maximum possible value of $\\frac{CT \\cdot NB}{BT \\cdot NE}$. Let $\\alpha$ denote the smallest real number such that for all sufficiently large $n$, $a_{2n} \u003c \\alpha$. Given that $\\alpha = p + \\sqrt{q}$ for rationals $p$ and $q$, what is the remainder when $\\left\\lfloor p^{q^p} \\right\\rfloor$ is divided by $99991$?\n"}
